.TH ZIMANYAR 1 "November 2026" "Zimanyar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zimanyar \- check and learn Kurdish on the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zimanyar check
.RI [ file ...| \- ]
.RB [ \-\-lang " ckb|kmr|auto]"
.RB [ \-\-format " text|json|sarif]"
.RB [ \-\-fix ]
.RB [ \-\-rules " list]"
.RB [ \-\-disable " list]"
.RB [ \-\-fail\-on " error|warning|hint|never]"
.RB [ \-\-tolerant ]
.RB [ \-\-markdown ]
.RB [ \-\-dictionary " file]"
.br
.B zimanyar analyze
.I word
.br
.B zimanyar conjugate
.I infinitive
.br
.B zimanyar decline
.I noun
.RB [ \-\-gender " f|m]"
.br
.B zimanyar
.BR ipa | translit | normalize | lid
.RI [ text ...| \- ]
.br
.B zimanyar explain
.I rule\-id
.br
.B zimanyar lesson
.RI [ number | rule\-id | words ]
.RB [ \-\-lang " ckb|kmr]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Zimanyar finds mistakes in Sorani and Kurmanji, explains each one, and teaches the grammar behind it.
It runs entirely on your own computer: nothing is ever sent anywhere, and no command opens a network
connection.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Check files, or standard input when no file or \- is given. Each paragraph is checked as Sorani or
Kurmanji, chosen by its script and words unless
.B \-\-lang
says which. Files ending in .md, .markdown or .mdx are checked in their prose only: code, links,
HTML and front matter are left alone, and reported lines and columns are those of the file.
.TP
.B analyze
Every reading of a word: lemma, part of speech, its parts and their features, best first.
.TP
.B conjugate
Every form of a verb, from its infinitive. A verb that is not in the core list is built from the
infinitive.
.TP
.B decline
Every form of a noun. A Kurmanji noun is declined in its gender from
.BR \-\-gender ,
from the lexicon, or in both when neither knows it.
.TP
.B ipa
The pronunciation of a text, in the International Phonetic Alphabet.
.TP
.B translit
A text in the other script: Sorani in Latin letters, Kurmanji in Arabic script.
.TP
.B normalize
A text with its letters, digits and spacing corrected to the written standard.
.TP
.B lid
Which language a text is in, and how sure the guess is.
.TP
.B explain
A rule's message and reason, with examples and the lessons that teach it.
.TP
.B lesson
Read a lesson in the terminal. With no topic, list every lesson. A topic is a lesson number, a rule
id, or words found in titles, then in the lessons themselves.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-format " text|json|sarif"
How
.B check
reports. JSON has lines and columns from 1, offsets, messages, suggestions and lessons. SARIF 2.1.0
suits code scanning; its columns count UTF\-16 code units.
.B analyze ,
.B conjugate
and
.B decline
also take
.BR "\-\-format json" .
.TP
.B \-\-fix
Apply the safe fixes, which change only spelling to the written standard, and write each file back.
With standard input, the corrected text goes to standard output and what is left to correct to
standard error.
.TP
.BR \-\-rules " list"
Run only these rules, comma separated. An entry names a rule, or every rule whose id starts with it,
such as
.B kmr.ergative
or
.BR ckb .
.TP
.BR \-\-disable " list"
Leave these rules out, named in the same way.
.TP
.BR \-\-fail\-on " error|warning|hint|never"
The least severe finding that makes the exit code 1. The default is
.BR error .
.TP
.B \-\-tolerant
Accept what is common in writing but outside the written standard.
.TP
.B \-\-markdown
Treat the input as Markdown, for standard input or a file with another name.
.TP
.BR \-\-dictionary " file"
Accept the words of a personal dictionary as spelled right: the JSON list the extension and the
desktop app export, or a text file with one word on each line, where # starts a comment. May be
given more than once.
.TP
.BR \-\-ui " en|ckb|kmr"
The language of messages and help. Without it, ZIMANYAR_UI and then the locale decide: ckb_IQ is
Sorani, ku_TR Kurmanji.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Help for Zimanyar, or for one command.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
The version of Zimanyar and of its data.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Nothing at or above the
.B \-\-fail\-on
severity was found, or a command other than check succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Findings at or above the
.B \-\-fail\-on
severity.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error: an unknown command, option, value, rule or file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ZIMANYAR_UI
The language of messages, as for
.BR \-\-ui .
.TP
.B ZIMANYAR_DATA
A folder with lexicon\-ckb.bin.gz and lexicon\-kmr.bin.gz, used before the lexicons the program
carries.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turn colour off. Colour is used only when standard output is a terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
zimanyar check \-\-lang kmr \-\-format json README.ku.md
zimanyar check \-\-format sarif docs/*.md > zimanyar.sarif
echo "Min tu dîtim." | zimanyar check
zimanyar conjugate dîtin
zimanyar lesson ergativity
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://0xdolan.github.io/Zimanyar/
